<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ComplianceOverrides>
  <!--
  VCF Content Factory Compliance: overrides file TEMPLATE.

  DO NOT EDIT THIS FILE. COPY IT.
  The pack installs and upgrades this template, so an upgrade can replace
  it. Your copy has a name the pack never uses, so no upgrade touches it.

  How to use it:
  1. In VCF Operations, open Infrastructure Operations > Configurations >
     Management Packs Configuration.
  2. Clone compliance_overrides_template (under System Defined). The
     dialog suggests compliance_overrides_template.xml_Copy; replace it
     with your own name ending in .xml, for example
     compliance_overrides_vc01.xml, and save. The copy appears under
     User Defined. One copy can serve several vCenters.
  3. Edit the copy: remove the comment markers around the entries you
     want and change the values.
  4. Edit the compliance account (Administration > Integrations >
     Accounts) and set Overrides file to the copy's name, without .xml.
  5. Wait one collection cycle. The vCenter object's property
     VCF-CF Compliance|Summary|overrides_status reads OK when the file
     loaded.

  Control ids (for example esx.account-lockout-max-attempts) are listed in
  the pack's REFERENCE.md and in the bundled profiles
  (profiles/canonical/scg_*.csv, column control_id). They are also the
  middle part of each metric under VCF-CF Compliance on the object.

  Control ids, element names (Skip, Override, Profile) and attribute
  names (control, expected, version, kind) are case-sensitive:
  ESX.ACCOUNT-LOCKOUT-DURATION or <skip> is rejected, not applied.

  A wrong entry (unknown control id, bad value, unknown version) is
  rejected and reported. The rest of the file still applies.
  -->

  <!--
  SKIP: turn a control off.
  No alert, not in the score. Every collection sets its metric to not
  evaluated (-1), so an open alert clears within three collections, and
  its Actual property reads "(skipped by override file <your file name>)".

  <Skip control="esx.account-lockout-max-attempts"/>
  -->

  <!--
  OVERRIDE: score against your value instead of the guide's value.
  The value must suit the control: a whole number for a number control,
  true or false for a true/false control, any text for a text control.
  On a text advanced setting, NULL and a blank quoted value are rejected,
  and "" (set, but empty) is accepted only where the guide's own value is
  empty (esx.network-dvfilter).
  These forms also work:
    (non-empty)       compliant when the setting has any value
    not:X             compliant when the setting has a value other than X
    vmx-N or higher   compliant when the VM hardware version is vmx-N or
                      later, for example vmx-19 or higher (text controls
                      only; "or newer" also works)
    X or Undefined    compliant when the setting is X or not set
                      (advanced settings only)
    X or Not Present  the same as X or Undefined (advanced settings only)
    Not Present       compliant only when the setting is not set
                      (advanced settings only)
  On an advanced setting, a plain value (X without "or Undefined") means
  an object where the setting is not set FAILS. Many guide values for VM
  advanced settings read "TRUE or Undefined"; overriding one with plain
  TRUE makes the rule stricter, and unset VMs then fail.
  A value that does not suit the control is rejected and the guide's
  value is kept. The control's Expected property reads
  "<value> (site override)".

  Example: allow 5 failed logon attempts before an ESX account locks.

  <Override control="esx.account-lockout-max-attempts" expected="5"/>
  -->

  <!--
  PROFILE: pin the guide version instead of Auto (by version).
  Without kind, the pin applies to every object of this instance. With
  kind, it applies to that object kind only, and wins over a pin without
  kind.
  Versions: SCG 6.7, SCG 7.0, SCG 8.0, SCG 9.0, SCG 9.1
  Kinds: HostSystem, VirtualMachine, vCenter, ClusterComputeResource,
         DistributedVirtualSwitch, DistributedVirtualPortgroup

  <Profile version="SCG 9.0"/>
  <Profile kind="VirtualMachine" version="SCG 8.0"/>
  -->
</ComplianceOverrides>
